course: dictionary
lesson: 8398
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To know which meaning is meant, look at the context: the words and sentences around it. In «Afterwards Grandpa ruffles her hair», the context shows that ruffle is a gentle movement, not a fight.
explain: Test each meaning in the sentence. Grandpa cannot upset her hair in the way a person can be upset, so the meaning "to make messy" fits best. Ask yourself: what would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense?
explain: A word can also change its job. As a verb, ruffle is an action. As a noun, a ruffle is a thing: a frill on a dress or shirt. Phrases change meaning too. "Ruffle someone's feathers" means to upset someone a little, and it has nothing to do with real feathers.
fact: Ruffle is a verb, an action word, and also a noun, a thing word.
fact: «Ruffle» as a verb means to make something uneven or messy, like hair, feathers or water.
fact: «Ruffle» as a verb can also mean to annoy or upset someone a little.
fact: A «ruffle» as a noun is a strip of gathered cloth used as decoration, also called a frill.
fact: «Unruffled» means calm and not upset.
exercise: «Afterwards Grandpa ruffles her hair.» What does ruffles mean here? | To wash with soap | *To make messy | To cut very short | To tie in a bow
exercise: Mum says, «Don't ruffle his feathers before the meeting.» What does ruffle feathers mean? | *To upset someone a little | To make a loud noise | To pluck the feathers from a bird | To brush feathers neatly
exercise: «Her dress had a row of ruffles around the neck.» What is a ruffle here? | A type of drum | A kind of bird | A small wild animal | *A frill of gathered cloth
test: «The wind ruffled the water of the lake.» What does ruffled mean? | Painted blue | Made very hot | *Made uneven with small waves | Frozen solid
test: «Ella was unruffled when the teacher called her name.» What does unruffled mean? | Angry and loud | *Calm and not upset | Late for school | Covered in mud
exam: «Her shirt had ruffles down the front.» What does ruffles mean? | To make hair messy | A soft drum roll | To annoy someone | *A frill of cloth
